  {
    "subject": "physics",
    "question": "How does a pendulum exchange energy?",
    "firstWordsMs": 3739,
    "speech": [
      "It swaps between height and speed, keeping the total steady.\n",
      "At the highest point of its swing, the pendulum momentarily pauses, so all its energy is stored as gravitational potential energy. As gravity pulls the bob downward, it accelerates, converting that potential energy into kinetic energy. When it reaches the lowest point, it moves fastest and all of that energy has turned into kinetic energy, which carries it back up the opposite side to trade speed for height again. Does that make sense?"
    ],
