  {
    "subject": "vectors",
    "question": "How do I add two vectors?",
    "firstWordsMs": 3281,
    "speech": [
      "You place the tail of the second vector at the head of the first.\n",
      "To add vectors graphically, slide the second vector without rotating it so its start sits directly on the arrow tip of the first. The total, or resultant vector, is the straight line drawn from the starting point of the first vector to the final tip of the second. \n\nIf you are working with numbers in component form, like horizontal and vertical parts, you simply add their corresponding x-components together and their y-components together."
    ],
