  {
    "subject": "calculus",
    "question": "What does a derivative mean?",
    "firstWordsMs": 2489,
    "speech": [
      "It measures how fast something is changing at a specific moment. Let me draw that for you.\n",
      "When you look at a curve, the slope changes at every point. The derivative gives you the exact slope of the tangent line touching the curve right at that single point. \n\nFor instance, if the curve represents your position over time, the derivative at any instant tells you your exact speedometer reading. Does that visual make sense?"
