    "question": "How did Roman roads help trade?",
    "firstWordsMs": 5269,
    "speech": [
      "Roman roads sped up trade by letting merchants move goods safely and quickly between cities.\n",
      "These paved, all-weather routes cut down travel time significantly and linked inland agricultural hubs directly to major ports and markets. Because the military patrolled them regularly, merchants could transport valuable cargo like grain, olive oil, and wine with far less risk of banditry."
